    "reason": "[ev-989a451dfcd4] names the subject (the StripPrefix middleware's `forceSlash` option) and the change (removed). It is a single line in a list of removals and says nothing about what happens to a configuration that still sets the option: whether it is ignored, rejected or breaks startup. The deterministic CRD check refuted the removal: it found that traefik.io Middleware spec.stripPrefix.forceSlash is still in the v3.0.0 schema [ev-0842f8f3bd9d]. So it is also unclear which configuration surface (CRD or file/other providers) actually lost the field, and who is exposed. A linked PR or reference docs saying where the option was removed and how leftover settings are handled are needed.",
